From: =?UTF-8?q?Vin=C3=ADcius=20Ferr=C3=A3o?= <2031761+viniciusferrao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/23] Reject STATUS for a section the file does not have

handle_status() turns the section number of a STATUS into an offset in
naklist, which holds one byte for each block of the file. It did not
check the section, so a receiver in the session that sent a section
past the end of the file made the server write past naklist. Reject
such a STATUS.
---
 server_transfer.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server_transfer.c b/server_transfer.c
index 65c9131..64bdb53 100644
--- a/server_transfer.c
+++ b/server_transfer.c
@@ -489,6 +489,11 @@ void handle_status(const unsigned char *message, unsigned meslen,
                      ntohs(status->file_id), finfo->file_id );
         return;
     }
+    if (section >= finfo->sections) {
+        glog1(finfo, "Rejecting STATUS from %s: invalid section %d",
+                     destlist[hostidx].name, section);
+        return;
+    }
 
     tfmcc = NULL;
     if (status->hlen * 4U > sizeof(struct status_h)) {
